1.8 Complete System Diagram
System Architecture Components
Frontend Layer
•	React.js frontend application
•	User dashboards and interfaces
Backend Layer
•	Node.js and Express.js REST APIs
•	Authentication and business logic
Database Layer
MongoDB database with:
•	users collection
•	licenses collection
•	licenserequests collection
Cloud Infrastructure
•	AWS EC2 Instances
•	AWS Application Load Balancer
•	AWS CloudWatch Monitoring
DevOps and Deployment
•	GitHub Repository
•	GitHub Actions CI/CD Pipeline
•	PM2 Process Manager
System Interaction Flow
1.	Users access the React frontend using a web browser.
2.	Frontend sends API requests to the Node.js/Express backend.
3.	Backend processes requests and communicates with MongoDB.
4.	Application is hosted on AWS EC2 instances.
5.	AWS Application Load Balancer distributes incoming traffic.
6.	AWS CloudWatch monitors system performance and availability.
7.	GitHub Actions automates CI/CD deployment workflows.

